k in  those days  are there are there problems still yes  but here i am and we are overcoming  america is becoming more and more we  have a saying in church you know i may  not be what i'm supposed to be but i  ain't what i used to be and that's  america so we're coming back to the  judgeships you know it really isn't  unheard of for america to to pick  certain people to to be on the the  supreme court you know we did it when we  wanted we clamored for a female judge  and we got sanjay o'connor that was a  good thing we clam it for a black judge  and we got thurgood marshall that was a  good thing and here we have a latina  judge and uh we have sonia sotomayor you  know it might not be the politics that  we like but we have her and and uh so  and and then  for the first hundred years of the  supreme court's history  those people expected the court to be  partisan and in fact they were highly  partisan so what i'm hoping is that the  president will bring us a judge you know  if she's black will bring us a judge who  respects the constitution and will  uphold the laws and will not be a  partisan  you know who will judge fairly most  importantly that's what we need  that's what we all need and what we all  want lieutenant governor as you're  speaking i'm getting the chills we know  that we will be following your journey  and this will not be your last stop on  the journey  lieutenant governor it's great to have  you this morning please come back soon  thank you so much for your leadership  thank you for having me and please pray  for our troops who are already in poland  and  you know i know there is a time for  peace and a time for war but let's hope  that we don't have to go to war  well said thank you so much lieutenant  governor  winsome sears

